1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:04,084
Most trading demos begin with a chart going up and to the right.

2
00:00:04,084 --> 00:00:06,912
Ours does too. The difference is what happens next.

3
00:00:07,332 --> 00:00:14,046
Finly's strongest retrospective nonproduction shadow combined a QQQ core with rotating sector momentum.

4
00:00:14,046 --> 00:00:20,760
In the consumed ETF replay from 2 January 2013 through 27 August 2026,

5
00:00:20,760 --> 00:00:24,376
with a modeled five-basis-point one-way turnover cost,

6
00:00:24,376 --> 00:00:30,574
it recorded an 18.97 percent annualized return against 15.11 percent for SPY,

7
00:00:30,574 --> 00:00:33,156
with a shallower maximum drawdown.

8
00:00:33,576 --> 00:00:36,691
Finly still refused to promote it.

9
00:00:36,691 --> 00:00:40,324
Its Deflated Sharpe probability was 3.75 percent,

10
00:00:40,324 --> 00:00:43,958
the worst adjusted familywise p-value was 0.3718,

11
00:00:43,958 --> 00:00:47,592
and the growth-control and source-overlap gates failed.

12
00:00:48,012 --> 00:00:50,080
That refusal is the product.

13
00:00:50,080 --> 00:00:53,803
AI may assess bounded evidence and explain a view.

14
00:00:53,803 --> 00:00:57,526
Code still owns direction, horizon, spread construction, maximum loss,

15
00:00:57,526 --> 00:01:02,076
and every Alpaca field. The llama does not get the keys.

16
00:01:02,496 --> 00:01:05,870
Code removes evidence families, perturbs market inputs,

17
00:01:05,870 --> 00:01:09,726
and recomputes the order. If the conclusion changes,

18
00:01:09,726 --> 00:01:14,064
Finly fails closed. A plausible rationale is not permission.

19
00:01:14,484 --> 00:01:17,727
Two synthetic receipts make the boundary visible.

20
00:01:17,727 --> 00:01:19,117
With aligned evidence,

21
00:01:19,117 --> 00:01:23,286
four source removals and thirty-two perturbations preserved the decision.

22
00:01:23,286 --> 00:01:26,992
With conflicting evidence, removing one source changed it,

23
00:01:26,992 --> 00:01:29,772
so the compiler returned no trade.

24
00:01:30,192 --> 00:01:32,179
When a fixture survives,

25
00:01:32,179 --> 00:01:37,146
code constructs a defined-risk bear-put spread and calculates the payoff.

26
00:01:37,146 --> 00:01:42,610
Here, maximum loss is 366 dollars and maximum gain is 634.

27
00:01:42,610 --> 00:01:46,584
The Alpaca-shaped payload is compiled but never transmitted.

28
00:01:47,004 --> 00:01:52,255
The chart is an ETF replay, not options profit and loss.

29
00:01:52,255 --> 00:01:55,596
The 113-item ledger includes controls, invalidated runs,

30
00:01:55,596 --> 00:01:57,983
and reruns—not 113 independent strategies.

31
00:01:57,983 --> 00:02:00,369
Seven later challengers promoted none.

32
00:02:00,369 --> 00:02:04,188
Reporting the limits is part of the result.

33
00:02:04,608 --> 00:02:07,764
G4 is not the production book.

34
00:02:07,764 --> 00:02:11,972
Production Finly is the lower-risk time-series-momentum volatility ensemble.

35
00:02:11,972 --> 00:02:14,602
In its now-consumed fixed holdout,

36
00:02:14,602 --> 00:02:19,862
it returned 11.13 percent annualized against 19.19 percent for SPY,

37
00:02:19,862 --> 00:02:24,596
with annualized volatility of 8.31 percent against 17.33 percent,

38
00:02:24,596 --> 00:02:30,908
and a maximum drawdown of minus 5.79 percent against minus 18.76 percent.

39
00:02:30,908 --> 00:02:35,642
Forward Trial One remains at zero of 252 settlements,

40
00:02:35,642 --> 00:02:38,798
so there is no next-month inference.

41
00:02:38,798 --> 00:02:42,480
Broker authority and performance inference remain disabled.

42
00:02:42,900 --> 00:02:45,420
Finly's contribution is not a bigger forecast.

43
00:02:45,420 --> 00:02:49,380
It is a smaller trust boundary: evidence may inform a trade,

44
00:02:49,380 --> 00:02:52,980
but verified authority must permit it. The bull has horns.

45
00:02:52,980 --> 00:02:55,860
The llama still does not get the keys.
